<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A CONTROL'S FEEDBACK, BOUNDED TO THE CONTROL. For the icon affordances that sit ON a
  card — the subscription card's chevron, ping, refresh, pin and Telegram.

  IT IS NO LONGER A RIPPLE, and the history is worth keeping because it is the same
  defect twice, from two directions.

  First it was ?attr/selectableItemBackgroundBorderless, which is `<ripple>` with NO
  layers at all. A RippleDrawable with no layers is UNBOUNDED: it neither clips to its
  own view nor stops at it, drawing a disc sized off the view's larger side and
  projecting onto the nearest ancestor that has a background. On this card that
  ancestor is the card, so one tap on a 22dp chevron lit a 20dp-radius card corner to
  corner:

      «кнопка скрытия раскрытия слишком сильно подсвечивается слишком огромный свет
       появляется при нажатии»

  A mask layer fixed the AREA — bounded, inside the control's own box — but not the
  KIND. The handoff README's «Главное правило» removes the kind: «В сборке нет ... ripple
  как отклика на нажатие». What the owner objected to was light appearing around a
  control, and a smaller splash is still a splash.

  So it is a state list now: while the finger is down, an oval of
  ?attr/colorPressBg fills the control's own box, and nothing animates outward from the
  touch point. Pair it with @anim/press_icon 0.88 on the same view — §1's borderless-icon
  rung — and the affordance is pushed IN rather than lit up. The oval is kept because
  these controls are square boxes holding a round glyph, and a rectangular plate inside a
  round affordance reads as a rendering fault.

  Fades on the press clock (70 in / 200 out), so the plate and the scale move together.
-->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:enterFadeDuration="@integer/motion_press_in"
    android:exitFadeDuration="@integer/motion_press_out">
    <item android:state_pressed="true">
        <shape android:shape="oval">
            <solid android:color="?attr/colorPressBg" />
        </shape>
    </item>
    <item android:state_focused="true">
        <shape android:shape="oval">
            <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
            <stroke
                android:width="@dimen/stroke_focus"
                android:color="?attr/colorPrimary" />
        </shape>
    </item>
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="oval">
            <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
        </shape>
    </item>
</selector>
